{"id": "EUVD-2026-78208", "enisaUuid": "6e46156e-2afa-3b24-9b92-e75179037aef", "description": "Refly through 1.1.0 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in the POST /v1/misc/scrape endpoint that fetches caller-supplied URLs without validating the scheme, host, or resolved address. Authenticated attackers can make the backend issue requests to loopback, private, and link-local addresses including cloud metadata services to read page titles and descriptions of internal resources.", "datePublished": "2026-09-14T22:10:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:22:16", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/refly-ai/refly/issues/2280", "https://github.com/refly-ai/refly", "https://github.com/refly-ai/refly/blob/77fb0ca184251bba7380cbac2dbdf7a6c9944652/packages/utils/src/scrape-weblink.ts", "https://github.com/refly-ai/refly/blob/77fb0ca184251bba7380cbac2dbdf7a6c9944652/apps/api/src/modules/misc/misc.controller.ts#L38-L43", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/refly-through-1.1.0-server-side-request-forgery-via-scrape-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-91199", "GHSA-8jjj-988v-wwgg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ffb30f7-cf6a-3a13-a3c5-d7a436ebb2df", "product": {"name": "refly", "vendor": {"name": "refly-ai"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a5222a1b-b055-3596-a12a-2642991c73c6", "vendor": {"name": "refly-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}